if (lowerBound == null) {
  return ROWS_CANNOT_MATCH; // values are all null
}
</code></pre> <p>A missing lower bound excludes the manifest. That looks like the opposite of the safe direction — until you recall section 5: <code>min</code> is only ever left null when no ordinary value was seen, so an absent bound is a proof that the partition column is entirely null (or entirely NaN), and <code>x &lt; 5</code> cannot match a null. The soundness of this branch is a consequence of how <code>PartitionFieldStats.update</code> is written, and nothing else.</p> <p><code>notNaN</code> is the same argument in a subtler form. It excludes only when <code>containsNaN</code> is true, <code>containsNull</code> is false, and <code>lowerBound</code> is null — three conditions that together mean "every value here is NaN". Any one of them missing, and the answer is "might".</p>

